        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Purpose."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " A detailed, citation‑backed study reference for the standard schedule of well‑child (health‑supervision) visits, for a PA student on a pediatrics rotation. For each visit age it gives four things: "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "(1) General WCC — what's done at the visit"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (history, measurements, exam focus, screenings/labs due, immunizations due); "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "(2) Things to look for"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (assessment focus and age‑specific red flags); "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "(3) Developmental milestones / expectations"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "; and "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "(4) Parent education / anticipatory guidance."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
