       }
      ],
      "text": "Accuracy & sourcing."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Every factual statement is tagged to an authoritative, current primary source and was retrieved on "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "2026‑10‑28"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". Sources are the AAP "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Bright Futures"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 4th edition (visit content) and the AAP/Bright Futures "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Recommendations for Preventive Pediatric Health Care"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " periodicity schedule (updated "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "February 2025"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "); the "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CDC \"Learn the Signs. Act Early.\" developmental milestones"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " (February 2022 revision, developed with the AAP); and the "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CDC/ACIP Child & Adolescent Immunization Schedule, United States, 2025."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Nothing here is written from memory. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Treat any item marked FLAG / UNCERTAIN as something to confirm against the primary source before applying it clinically"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — and remember that studying from this document is not the same as fact‑checking it against the source."
     }
